 "comments": [
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "24911101"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "36610787"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Catalyzes the hydrolysis of queuosine 5'-phosphate, releasing the nucleobase queuine (q). Is required for salvage of queuine from exogenous queuosine (Q) that is imported and then converted to queuosine 5'-phosphate intracellularly. In vitro, can also catalyze the release of the q base directly from Q as substrate; however, it was shown that Q is not the biologically relevant substrate. Shows a very low activity on queuosine 3',5'-diphosphate, and cannot release q from queuosine 3'-phosphate and from the 5'-nucleotides AMP, UMP, CMP or GMP, indicating specificity for the queuine base (PubMed:36610787). Can complement the yeast mutant SPAC589.05c, restoring Q incorporation into tRNA (PubMed:24911101)"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "FUNCTION"
  },
  {
   "commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY",
   "reaction": {
