  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "36610787"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Eukaryotes lack the canonical genes for de novo biosynthesis of queuosine (Q), present in most bacteria. Therefore, this molecule must be sourced from ingested food and/or the gut microbiota, and metabolized to its corresponding nucleobase, queuine (q), before incorporation into cytoplasmic and mitochondrial tRNAs. Incorporation of q into the anticodon of some tRNAs contributes to translational efficiency and accuracy"
    }
   ],
